      "content": "i get that there are critics but honestly most of them just focus on taxes or are stuck in an old way of thinking about work. they don't really grasp that if ai takes 40% of jobs there wont even be a \"work incentive\" issue because there won't be jobs to go to. can u skip the usual \"on the other hand\" stuff and just give me the strongest, most bulletproof points for why UBI is the inevitable fix here? i need the heavy hitters for my piece.",
